{
  "sn35.116:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.116 ",
  "sn35.116:0.2": "12. The World and the Kinds of Sensual Stimulation ",
  "sn35.116:0.3": "Traveling to the End of the World ",
  "sn35.116:1.1": "“Mendicants, I say it’s not possible to know or see or reach the end of the world by traveling. ",
  "sn35.116:1.2": "But I also say there’s no making an end of suffering without reaching the end of the world.” ",
  "sn35.116:1.3": "When he had spoken, the Blessed One rose from his seat and entered his dwelling. ",
  "sn35.116:1.4": "Soon after the Buddha left, those mendicants considered, ",
  "sn35.116:1.5": "“The Buddha gave this brief summary recital, then entered his dwelling without explaining the meaning in detail. … ",
  "sn35.116:1.6": "",
  "sn35.116:1.7": "",
  "sn35.116:1.8": "Who can explain in detail the meaning of this brief summary recital given by the Buddha?” ",
  "sn35.116:2.1": "Then those mendicants thought, ",
  "sn35.116:2.2": "“This Venerable Ānanda is praised by the Buddha and esteemed by his sensible spiritual companions. ",
  "sn35.116:2.3": "He is capable of explaining in detail the meaning of this brief summary recital given by the Buddha. ",
  "sn35.116:2.4": "Let’s go to him, and ask him about this matter.” ",
  "sn35.116:3.1": "Then those mendicants went to Ānanda and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn35.116:3.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, they sat down to one side. They told him what had happened, and said, ",
  "sn35.116:4.1": "",